\description{
\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#experimental}{\figure{lifecycle-experimental.svg}{options: alt='[Experimental]'}}}{\strong{[Experimental]}}

\code{\link[=update_sp_list_person_items]{update_sp_list_person_items()}} is a variant of
\code{\link[=update_sp_list_lookup_items]{update_sp_list_lookup_items()}} for person or group columns. Person or group
columns are a type of lookup column where the lookup list is the hidden
"User Information List" for the site. By default, users are matched by email
address (ignoring case). Users that have never accessed the site are not
included in the "User Information List" and can't be matched.
}
\details{
\code{\link[=create_sp_list_lookup_column]{create_sp_list_lookup_column()}} is a wrapper for \code{\link[=create_lookup_column]{create_lookup_column()}}
and \code{\link[=create_sp_list_column]{create_sp_list_column()}} that creates a lookup column in a list
(\code{sp_list}) using a column from a second list in the same site (the "lookup"
list). \code{\link[=create_sp_list_person_column]{create_sp_list_person_column()}} is a wrapper for
\code{\link[=create_person_column]{create_person_column()}} and \code{\link[=create_sp_list_column]{create_sp_list_column()}} that creates a person
or group column.

\code{\link[=fmt_sp_list_lookup_items]{fmt_sp_list_lookup_items()}} formats one or more lookup (or person or group)
columns in \code{data} by replacing the values with matching lookup list item ID
values and renaming the columns to \code{"{column_name}LookupId"}. Use the output
with \code{\link[=create_sp_list_items]{create_sp_list_items()}} or \code{\link[=update_sp_list_items]{update_sp_list_items()}}.

Values in \code{data} that can't be matched to a lookup list item are listed in a
message and replaced with \code{NA} values. Missing values are never matched.
}
